{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"ROOT-CAUSE INSIGHT FROM THE IMPLEMENTER, better than my framing and worth pinning: 'make check' ALREADY IS the fast tier (lint + typecheck), and its help text -- 'Run every check-only gate (no mutation)' -- IS ITSELF HOW THE FALSE GREEN ACQUIRED ITS AUTHORITY. A contributor reads 'every check-only gate', runs it, sees green, and reasonably concludes they have verified. The defect is not only that some gates live in pytest; it is that an existing target CLAIMS completeness it does not have.\n\nSo the fix corrects that claim rather than minting a third target name. Quoting the reasoning, which I think is right: 'Adding one would build a menu, and a menu invites picking the cheap item; deleting a false claim from an existing target shrinks the surface instead of growing it.' That is a better answer than the fast-tier option I floated, and it means my suggestion would have grown the surface that produced the problem.\n\nMEASUREMENT DISQUALIFIED THE OBVIOUS DEFAULT: '-n auto' reached 7% in ~8 minutes on this host (18 logical / 6 performance cores), extrapolating past 100 MINUTES, because a large share of this suite forks git/bash/pytest subprocesses and oversubscribes. '-n 4 --dist worksteal' tracks to ~14 minutes; the recorded serial local suite is 1726s (~29 min). Notably the repo had ALREADY decided this -- _build-and-test.yml:780 records the explicit decision against -n auto ('over-subscribes on larger local hosts') and docs/coverage.md:42-47 already tells contributors to use -n 4. The measurement confirmed existing reasoning rather than discovering something new, which is the cheapest kind of confirmation and worth doing anyway.\n\nPLAN REVIEW CAUGHT A REAL GAP: changing make test's scheduler without enumerating the docs that describe its serial behaviour. Now enumerated -- docs/local-dev-env.md:466 and docs/coverage.md:36-47 updated, with :470-483 deliberately left alone because it contrasts coverage tracing and tier breadth rather than scheduling, and already quotes -n 4.\n\nAND THE IMPLEMENTER CORRECTED ITS OWN COMPLETENESS ARGUMENT: DEFAULT_SUITE_MARKS is matrix-CONDITIONAL, not the flat string first claimed. Restated precisely -- make test exactly matches the gating ubuntu-latest/py3.13 cell, is a strict superset of the other two Ubuntu cells (which add 'and not repo_policy'), and a superset of macOS's platform_compat subset. The by-construction completeness claim survives and is now accurate rather than approximately right."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788514091879342001,"uuid":"6ab6be18-e63e-440f-ac03-2424faabb893"}